+
+ ## Graduation gate
+
+ A4 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:
+
+ 1. **Low-quality decision rate** ≤ 10%: `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`.
+ 2. **Audit coverage**: every decision is audited in shadow mode (sampling rate = 1.0).
+ 3. **Budget violation response**: `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when rate > 10% (criterion 4.14).
+ 4. **Per-turn cumulative budget**: A4 is the first to degrade (degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1).
+
+ ## Out of scope
+
+ - Post-promotion sampling (OQ-004, Stage 5).
+ - Decision quality scoring model (Stage 5 enhancement).
+
+ ## A04 re-verification (2026-11-01, TF-0296)
+
+ The four gate limits above are the original ones and were **not redefined**. A04 only
+ re-mapped each criterion to executable evidence, fixed the `requiredTests` drift, and
+ recorded the gaps it could not close. Details:
+ `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md`.
+
+ - **Offline / dev-tool-only by design.** `docs/runtime-design/development-manual.md` §1.4
+   ("A4 — Decision Quality (offline pure functions only)") states A4 "is called ONLY via
+   explicit dev-tool invocation (CLI, test fixture, debug panel)" and "does NOT depend on
+   any other area at runtime". `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/decision-quality-auditor.ts`
+   therefore has **no production caller**; the production audit-coverage half of the
+   Active Pilot gate stays **NO-GO** by design, not by missing implementation.
+ - **Criterion 1/3 evidence.** `DecisionQualityAuditor.auditBatch()` charges
+   `deprecationCounters` one audited decision per record (sampling rate 1.0), and
+   `checkBudgetViolation("a4")` returns `degrade_to_audit_only` only when
+   `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions > 0.10`. Asserted by
+   `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`, the `a4` branch of
+   `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, and `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`.
+ - **Criterion 4 order evidence.** `spanDropPriority()` in
+   `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/namespace-governance.ts` orders
+   `core < a6 < a1 < a2 < a5 < a3 < a4`, so A4 spans are dropped before A3, A5 and A1;
+   asserted by `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` and
+   `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts`. A4 never runs on a production turn, so
+   the per-turn cumulative latency **number** is NOT-MEASURED (NO-GO).
+ - **`requiredTests` drift fixed.** The original list named only
+   `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` and `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`,
+   which left criteria 2 and 4 without a named assertion. The auditor, a4-deep and
+   truncation-order tests are now listed, together with the A04 coverage guard
+   `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts`. Tests listed above but missing from this
+   re-verification snapshot are declared in `evidenceGaps`.
